Body:
can confirm this behaviour. I'm on Mac, latest opencode version:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "model": "github-copilot/claude-haiku-4.5",
  "small_model": "github-copilot/gpt-5-mini",
  "agent": {
    "explore": {
      "model": "github-copilot/claude-haiku-4.5",
      "options": {},
      "permission": {}
    },
    "title": {
      "model": "github-copilot/gpt-5-mini",
      "options": {},
      "permission": {}
    },
    "compaction": {
      "model": "github-copilot/gpt-5-mini",
      "options": {},
      "permission": {}
    }
  },
  "mcp": {
    "context7": {
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://mcp.context7.com/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "CONTEXT7_API_KEY": "..."
      }
    }
  },
  "formatter": {
    "charpier": {
      "command": [
        "dotnet",
        "csharpier",
        "format",
        "$FILE"
      ],
      "extensions": [
        ".cs"
      ]
    }
  },
  "compaction": {
    "auto": true,
    "prune": true,
    "reserved": 8000
  },
  "mode": {},
  "plugin": [],
  "command": {},
  "username": "..."
}
```

Can confirm in 1.2.25.  I have:
```jsonc
"agent": {
    "plan": {
      "model": "openrouter/google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview-customtools",
      "prompt": "{file:/home/risa/coding-config/plan.txt}",
      "tools": {
        "lsp": true
      },
      "permission": {
        "edit": {
          "*": "deny",
          ".agents/": "allow",
          ".agents/*.md": "allow"
        },
        "lsp": "allow"
      }
    } 
  }
```

but write to `.agents/` is still automatically denied:

<img width="1670" height="919" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9b4e8044-3828-4941-ba65-79b70a78aad9" />

Experimenting with the `"*"` catch all condition confirmed that the catch all condition is applying to everything for edit, and the matches that should take precedent did not.
